   "timed": true,
   "text": "Every city in Open World Chess is drawn by the hand that rules it. Blossomford, where a wide bridge carries the avenue over the river and into a garden square. Sunwall, a citadel in the desert, four gates on four roads, and a well at its heart. Pinehold, a ring of homes around a village green, its fields fenced against the forest. Stillwater, where the piers reach out across the lake, and the lamps come on at dusk. And Emberfort, a keep within a keep, walled against the strange lands. Streets and squares, bridges and walls, gardens and fields, and every piece fits every other. Open World Chess, the City Builder update. Build something beautiful."
